### ====================================================================
### PayVault — Review 1: Faculty Demo Checklist & REST Client Test
### Target: Eureka (:9000), Gateway (:8000), Auth (:8080), Wallet (:8082), Txn (:8083)
### ====================================================================

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8000
@authServiceUrl = http://localhost:8080
@walletServiceUrl = http://localhost:8082
@txnServiceUrl = http://localhost:8083

### ====================================================================
### 1. EUREKA / SERVICE DISCOVERY
### Open in browser: http://localhost:9000
### Verify Registered Instances:
###   - AUTHSERVICE1       -> 8080
###   - GATEWAYSERVICE     -> 8000
###   - TRANSACTIONSERVICE -> 8083
###   - WALLETSERVICE      -> 8082
### ====================================================================


### ====================================================================
### 2. JWT AUTHENTICATION
### ====================================================================

### 2.1 Register User (ReviewUser)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "ReviewUser",
    "email": "reviewuser@gmail.com",
    "password": "123456"
}

### 2.2 Register User (Ashish - Sender)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Ashish",
    "email": "ashish@gmail.com",
    "password": "123456"
}

### 2.3 Register User (Piyush - Receiver)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Piyush",
    "email": "piyush@gmail.com",
    "password": "123456"
}

### 2.4 Login (Ashish) -> Obtain JWT Token
# @name loginAshish
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "ashish@gmail.com",
    "password": "123456"
}

### Store Ashish's Bearer token for protected requests:
@jwtToken = {{loginAshish.response.body.token}}


### ====================================================================
### 3. WALLET SERVICE THROUGH GATEWAY
### ====================================================================

### 3.1 Get Wallet (User 1 - Ashish)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/wallet/1
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

### 3.2 Add Money (User 1 - Ashish: +1000)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/wallet/add/1?amount=1000
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

### 3.3 Check Balance (User 1 - Ashish: Should reflect updated balance)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/wallet/1
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}


### ====================================================================
### 4. TRANSACTION SERVICE THROUGH GATEWAY
### ====================================================================

### 4.1 Create Transaction (Transfer from Ashish [id: 1] to Piyush [id: 2])
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "senderId": 1,
    "receiverId": 2,
    "amount": 1000,
    "status": "SUCCESS"
}

### 4.2 Get All Transactions
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}


### ====================================================================
### 5. DIRECT SERVICE VS GATEWAY COMPARISON (Show Faculty)
### ====================================================================

### 5.1 DIRECT: Auth Service (:8080)
POST {{authServiceUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "ashish@gmail.com",
    "password": "123456"
}

### 5.2 THROUGH GATEWAY: Auth Service (:8000)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "ashish@gmail.com",
    "password": "123456"
}

### 5.3 DIRECT: Wallet Service (:8082)
GET {{walletServiceUrl}}/api/wallet/1

### 5.4 THROUGH GATEWAY: Wallet Service (:8000)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/wallet/1

### 5.5 DIRECT: Transaction Service (:8083)
GET {{txnServiceUrl}}/api/transactions

### 5.6 THROUGH GATEWAY: Transaction Service (:8000)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/transactions


### ====================================================================
### 6. POSTGRESQL — VERIFY DATABASE RECORDS
### Database: payvault (Port: 5433)
### Run in psql / DBeaver / pgAdmin:
###
### SELECT * FROM public.users ORDER BY id ASC;
### SELECT * FROM public.wallets ORDER BY id ASC;
### SELECT * FROM public.transactions ORDER BY id ASC;
### ====================================================================
